      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Approximately 50% of patients with peripheral vascular disease have severe coronary artery disease. Several ways of predicting the postoperative risk of major cardiac events in peripheral vascular patients have been suggested. Among preoperative tests, echocardiography is now receiving greater favor for risk stratification."},
